---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PriceBoard from '../components/PriceBoard.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Tire Services and Prices | Oakspur Tire & Wheel, Kansas City"
  description="Flat repair, mounting and balancing, rotations, alignments and tire pressure sensors in Kansas City, with every price posted."
>
  <section class="wrap page-head">
    <h1>Services and prices</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Everything we do has to do with tires and wheels. That's why a flat takes us half an hour and
      not half a day.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="band band--rubber">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <h2>The price board</h2>
        <p class="lede" style="margin-top:1rem">
          Prices are per car or light truck. Dually and oversize tires cost a little more, and we'll
          tell you how much before we start.
        </p>
      </div>
      <PriceBoard />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap split split--wide-right">
      <h2>What each job covers</h2>
      <ul class="ruled">
        <li>
          <h3>Flat repair</h3>
          <p>
            We take the tire off the wheel, check the inside, then plug and patch it from the inside
            out. A nail in the tread can usually be fixed. Damage in the sidewall can't be, and
            we'll show you why.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Mounting and balancing</h3>
          <p>
            For tires you bought somewhere else. We mount them, balance each wheel on the machine
            and torque the lug nuts by hand.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Rotation</h3>
          <p>
            Moving your tires front to back every 5,000 to 7,000 miles helps them wear evenly. It
            takes about 15 minutes, and it's free on tires from us.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Alignment</h3>
          <p>
            If your car pulls to one side or the steering wheel sits crooked, the alignment is
            likely off. We set all four wheels and hand you the before and after printout.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Tire pressure sensors</h3>
          <p>
            That horseshoe-shaped warning light means a tire is low or a sensor has died. We test
            all four, replace the bad one and reset the light.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Winter changeover</h3>
          <p>
            We swap your winter set on and off each season and mark where each tire came from so
            they go back in the right spot.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band--paper">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <h2>Is it time for new tires?</h2>
        <p class="lede" style="margin-top:1rem">Three checks you can do in your driveway.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="checks">
        <li>
          <h3>The penny test</h3>
          <p>
            Put a penny in the tread with Lincoln's head pointing down. If you can see the top of
            his head, the tread is worn out.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>The date code</h3>
          <p>
            Find the four digits after DOT on the sidewall. The first two are the week and the last
            two are the year. Tires older than six years are worth having checked.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Cracks and bulges</h3>
          <p>
            A bulge in the sidewall means the tire is damaged inside. Don't drive on it. Put the
            spare on or call us.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .checks {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: check;
  }

  .checks li {
    position: relative;
    padding: 1.35rem 0 1.35rem 3.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    counter-increment: check;
  }

  .checks li:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .checks li::before {
    content: counter(check);
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 1.1rem;
    width: 2.4rem;
    height: 2.4rem;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--rubber);
    color: var(--crayon);
    font-family: var(--marker);
    font-size: 1.3rem;
  }

  .checks h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .checks p {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
</style>
